# Line-ending normalization. The repository stores LF; checkouts on Windows may
# be CRLF. Several build/verify scripts compare generated files byte-for-byte
# (scripts/gen-preset.mjs --check, scripts/repack.ps1), so the rule has to be
# explicit rather than inherited from each machine's global core.autocrlf —
# with autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, `gen-preset --check` reported a
# permanent false STALE on a clean checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The generated bundle preset patch is compared byte-for-byte by gen-preset --check.
packages/helmd/preset.generated.patch.yml text eol=lf

# Not text: keep these byte-exact on every platform.
*.tgz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.asar binary

# ── fork: sealed distribution artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────
# These are generated by scripts/repack.ps1 (build-profiles + build-sealed) and
# are committed upstream so a fresh clone runs without a build step. They are
# AES-256-GCM blobs: a textual merge conflict in them is unmergeable, and every
# regeneration produces different bytes for identical plaintext (random IV).
#
# -diff          : never render them in diffs/review
# merge=ours     : a conflict resolves to the local side instead of leaving
#                  conflict markers inside a sealed blob
# Requires once per clone:  git config merge.ours.driver true
# After any merge, regenerate:  pwsh ./scripts/repack.ps1
packages/helmd/payload.dat        binary -diff merge=ours
packages/helmd/references.dat     binary -diff merge=ours
packages/helmd/presets/profiles.dat binary -diff merge=ours

# Fork-local dev helper (machine-specific node/pnpm paths).
_env.ps1 -text
